Comments: [Evaluator: Christian Iliadis; Date: xx/xx/2024]
1.  Measured resonance strengths are from Endt 1998; we assumed an uncertainty of 25% if no value is listed.
2.  Er = 73 keV [Ex = 11657 keV]: partial widths estimated from measured Gp [transfer], (a,g) strength, and Ga/G; Gp is obtained from the upper limit on the weak
    ell=0 component and the lower limit provided by the dominant ell=2 component of the transfer angular distribution. 
3.  Er = 86 keV [Ex = 11670 keV]: only an upper limit can be obtained from proton transfer for Gp; Gg and Ga are derived from the measured (a,g) strength and Ga/G. 
4.  Er = 195.07 keV [Ex = 11778.7 keV; 2+]: Gp and Gg are estimated from shell-model results; Ga is derived from the measured (a,g) strength, which belongs to this,
    natural parity, component of the doublet. The derived (p,g) strength is much smaller (factor 20) than the measured value for the doublet and, thus, the latter
    most likely belongs to the 5+ component.
5.  ENSDF 2013 lists a third level, at 11780.7 (0+ - 4+); we find no compelling evidence that this state is distinct from Ex = 11778.7 keV (2+). 
6.  Er = 216 keV [Ex = 11800 keV; (2,3)-]: we assume this level has unnatural parity since there is no evidence to the contrary.
7.  Er = 284 keV [Ex = 11867 keV; 4+]: Gp estimated from measured (p,g) strength; Gg = 1 eV is based on shell-model values of neighboring levels; Ga upper limit
    is derived from measured Ga/G upper limit.
8.  Er = 316 keV [Ex = 11900 keV; 4+]: Gp and Ga are derived from measured (p,g) and (a,g) strengths; Gg = 1 eV is an estimate based on shell-model results of
    neighboring levels.
9.  Er = 392 keV [Ex = 11976 keV; 4+]: Gp and Ga from measured (p,g) and (a,g) strengths; Gg = 1 eV estimate based on shell model values for neighboring levels.
10. Er = 439 keV [Ex = 12023 keV; 5-]: Gp upper limit from measured proton transfer spectrum; Gg = 1 eV is an approximate estimate based on shell-model results for 
    neighboring states.
11. Er = 0.99 keV [Ex = 11584 keV; 3-]: we shifted this resonance, slightly, below threshold for more stable computation; assuming Ga << Gg, the value of Ga can
    be derived from the measured (a,g) strength; Gg = 1 eV is an approximate estimate based on shell-model results for neighboring states.   
12. S factor of low-energy tails of broad resonances is estimated from known strengths and widths listed in Endt 1990. 
13. We assumed unnatural parity for the following levels with ambiguous Jp values (based on shell-model assignments): Ex = 11799.8, 11933.5, 11986, and 12015.8 keV 
    (Er = 216, 350, 402, and 432 keV).

